  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 200 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nThursday through Tuesday:\n\nHigh pressure remain in the region on Thursday with cooler and \ndrier conditions expected. Winds will back from the east to be \nfrom the south Friday into Saturday which will bring in moisture\nalong with higher temperatures with highs up to the low 90s by \nSunday afternoon and dewpoints near the low 70s. With these hot \nand humid conditions, the potential for rain and thunderstorms \nreturn by the end of the weekend into early next week.\n\nSunday into Monday, the next weather system will move through\nthe region and bring rain and thunderstorm chances. Severity of\nthese storm/rain chances will be determined by the timing of the\nsystem which is uncertain at this point, but will have more\nclarity by the end of the week. Hot and humid temps are \nexpected to continue into the beginning of next week along with \nincreased cloud coverage, but by Tuesday, winds will shift to be\nfrom the north as the system exits which will bring in cool and\ndrier air by mid week.\n\nSoergel/Kuroski",
